6. Dataset and Features
The default run creates 1,600 synthetic rows, balanced between normal and attack-like labels. A fixed random seed makes the example reproducible. The eight features are:

• duration_seconds — simulated duration of a flow.
• source_bytes and destination_bytes — simulated byte counts.
• packet_count — simulated packet count.
• failed_connection_rate — synthetic rate-like indicator.
• destination_port_risk — synthetic port-risk indicator.
• syn_packet_rate — synthetic SYN-rate indicator.
• bytes_per_packet — derived from byte counts and packet count.
The names are inspired by network-flow measurements, but the values do not come from packet captures or a real dataset. The generated attack-like class has intentionally distinctive patterns, so the task is easier than real intrusion detection.

7. Methodology
Data generation: Create normal and attack-like numeric samples using a fixed random state and shuffle the rows.

Split: Use a stratified 75% training / 25% test split with a fixed seed.

Preprocessing: Apply median imputation and standard scaling in a scikit-learn pipeline. The generated data has no missing values; imputation is included for pipeline completeness.

Training: Fit a RandomForestClassifier with 150 trees, a fixed random seed, and balanced class weights.

Evaluation: Predict held-out labels and calculate accuracy, attack-class precision, attack-class recall, F1-score, and a classification report.

Outputs: Save CSV and JSON/text metrics, a confusion-matrix plot, feature-importance plot, and serialized model.

